ing a daily record. Since 2000, Pendleton has set <strong>38 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 74 that chance alone would give, and <strong>58 record highs</strong>, close to the 74 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (69). Pendleton's all-time high is 119\u00b0F, on August 10, 1898.","t_chg":"Pendleton's nights warmed over the long run. Its days cooled over the long run but have warmed since 1986.","p_chg":"Across 120 complete years: Pendleton's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.23\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.15 to +0.31), about +3.0\u00b0F since 1895. Pendleton's average high has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.15\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.24 to \u22120.05), about \u22121.9\u00b0F since 1895. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows show no clear change and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.63\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.26 to +1.01). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 8 of 12 months. Highs rose in none; 6 months fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Pendleton's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.10 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 12.8 inches a year. The wettest year was 1899 (20.08 in); the driest, 1967 (6.77 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 2 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}